WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.160
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna,

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.860
and this is Geshe Michael Roach,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.830
and this is our third course

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.800
covering a very, very famous book.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.950
Maybe it's the most famous
Buddhist book after the Buddha,

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.350
and it's just called "Wisdom."

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.020
And it's by someone that
we call Arya Nagarjuna.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:26.020
Arya of course means that
he saw emptiness directly.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:31.170
And in fact, he's so famous
as a emptiness direct seer

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.160
that sometimes he's just called The Arya.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.343
He lived almost exactly 2000 years ago.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.800
And I think there may be
some interesting connections

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.800
between some Christian
saints: Thomas the disciple

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.006
who came to India and Nagarjuna.

00:00:50.006 --> 00:00:55.006
And he really took the
Buddhist teachings on emptiness

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.460
after 700 years, and he really,
really woke them up again.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:06.790
I think one of the
signs that he's an Arya,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.080
number one is he's funny
and he's just really clever

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.480
and funny when he presents things.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.480
Secondly, he really
enjoyed writing in poetry,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.030
and he's very, very simple.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.870
So I think that's also a sign

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.480
that he really did see emptiness directly.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:33.080
He prefers to speak very
simply, very clearly.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.930
It's almost like he's
singing a song when he wrote

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:41.300
his greatest book of all is
called, just simply, "Wisdom".

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.990
In Sanskrit, which we're
going to talk about later,

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.698
it's called Prajna.

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.340
I think that's another sign he's an Arya:

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:52.760
he just named his book "Wisdom."

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.360
And later people would say,
the root text on "Wisdom",

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.130
or Mūla madhyamaka kārikā,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.890
the verses of the root text on wisdom.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.120
But Nargajuna himself
preferred to call his book

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.300
just "Wisdom". How can we see emptiness?

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.460
How can I help you to see emptiness?

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:17.460
And that little book, 27
tiny chapters in poetry,

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:23.090
became, you know, for 2000 years,

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.160
hundreds of commentaries were written

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.230
about these simple 27 small verses.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.160
And it really, all the emptiness teachings

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.600
that you've ever heard,
that I've ever heard,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.490
all the emptiness
teachings in Tibet, China,

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:42.490
Korea, Japan, they're all
based on Nagarjuna's "Wisdom".

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:46.570
So I thought, about three years ago,

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.890
I was thinking it would
be a really nice break

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.890
during the Lam Rim if
we studied for dessert,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.460
if we studied Arya Nagarjuna's "Wisdom".

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:01.130
And recently we've been doing
Medicine Buddha practices,

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.780
especially because of the virus,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.980
and I thought it would
be really, really cool

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.170
if we connected Arya Nagarjuna's "Wisdom"

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.040
and the practice of Medicine Buddha.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.040
I personally feel strongly
that if you don't understand

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.610
the emptiness of the
Medicine Buddha practice,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:26.110
the emptiness of the
Medicine Buddha himself,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.850
and the emptiness of the
mantra of the Medicine Buddha,

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.160
then I don't think it will work so strong.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.710
It will work a little bit.

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.040
The mantras will work a little bit

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.213
and all the different practices
like meditation, retreat,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.430
saving the lives of animals,

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.230
these are all powerful practices.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.660
But if you really understand the emptiness

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.450
of these practices, if you
understand the emptiness

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:57.270
of saving someone's life, or
you understand the emptiness

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:01.483
of speaking of a mantra,
then in my opinion,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.680
the practice is a thousand
times more powerful.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.290
So we're going to go

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.273
through Nagarjuna's "Wisdom" together.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.400
Then from time to time,
we'll try to connect it

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.550
to the Medicine Buddha
practice and supercharge,

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.020
put an engine, extra booster,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.633
rocket booster on your
Medicine Buddha practice.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:30.640
My plan was to go through the
"Wisdom" text, 27 chapters,

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.270
in five years, probably
the greatest commentary

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.750
of many, many great
commentaries, for example,

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.873
by Chandrakirti,
Buddhapalita, Bhavaviveka,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.950
these great, great ancient
Indian commentaries.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.563
And then Tsongkapa came
along, I don't know,

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:55.970
1,200 years after Arya Nargajuna

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.217
and he wrote a book called
"The Sea of Emptiness,"

00:04:58.217 --> 00:05:00.020
"The Ocean of Emptiness."

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:04.380
And that's a great, great
commentary on the 27 verses.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.820
And then even Tsongkapa is very difficult.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.830
After that Choney Lama Drakpa Shedrup

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.710
about 200, 300 years after Tsongkapa,

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.487
he wrote a funny book called,

00:05:17.487 --> 00:05:20.650
"A Ship to Travel Across
the Sea of Emptiness".

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.130
It means Tsongkapa's, even
Tsongkapa's commentary's

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.670
too difficult.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.750
And we need like, Choney
Lama gives us a boat,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:31.320
so we don't drown in Tsongkapa's book.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.895
So we're going to be going through

00:05:33.895 --> 00:05:37.050
Choney Lama's explanation.
I'll be using that.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.080
And I'm translating it as we go.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.210
It's very difficult.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.220
The verses are very, very difficult.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.700
Without Choney Lama I don't think we could

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.693
understand Nagarjuna correctly.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:53.360
And so here we go.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.920
We're going to first review,
this first class is a review

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.060
of the chapters that we finished already.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:04.040
We did finish the first eight chapters

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.660
of Nagarjuna's "Wisdom".

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.580
And we're going to just
go through those today,

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:11.210
in this class, we'll go
through those eight chapters

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.470
and just review them together.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.157
The first chapter is called,

00:06:18.157 --> 00:06:21.640
"An Investigation of Conditions".

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.970
Each of the 27 chapters
is called pariksha.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:30.970
Pariksha means an investigation,
or an examination,

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.480
or an analysis of a certain topic.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:39.260
So Nagarjuna will take a certain idea

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.240
and in the first case here
we're talking about causes.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.990
What causes something else?

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:48.890
How does a seed work to cause a tree?

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:51.970
So that's the first chapter, the pariksha,

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.610
the examination or the investigation.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:59.500
And it feels like a Sherlock
Holmes investigation.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.053
How does this really work?

00:07:04.115 --> 00:07:06.790
How do seeds really create
trees and how do mantras

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:11.090
of Medicine Buddha cure a
disease to cure a sickness?

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.930
How does it really work?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:17.050
How do conditions work?
And in this first chapter,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:20.410
Nargajuna goes through the
four classic conditions

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:24.680
that are presented in the
Abhidharma before Nargajuna,

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:26.100
before Nargajuna came.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:30.490
So he's looking into causes.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:33.490
How does a mantra cure a disease

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:34.950
in the Medicine Buddha case?

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:39.500
How does a tree seed really create a tree?

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.130
And this is the pariksha.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.310
This is the first examination.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:48.310
The most famous lines of
"Wisdom" are found here.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.470
Actually, it's not even the first chapter.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:56.470
It's the traditional prostration
at the beginning of a book.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:01.800
So it's tradition to bow down
at the beginning of a great

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:05.020
Buddhist commentary, a great,
great Buddhist book, shastra

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:08.810
or sutra. You bow down to your teacher,

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:11.900
or you bow down to some holy object.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:16.900
And what Nargajuna chooses to
bow down to is always a sign

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:21.950
of what he's going to be
talking about for 27 chapters.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:26.650
Who does he choose to bow
down to at the beginning

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.380
of his book. And that verse, those verses,

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.730
those lines of his first bowing down

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.410
at the beginning of the book,

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.390
these are the most
famous lines by Nargajuna

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.730
and probably the most famous
lines ever about emptiness.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.890
So if you wanted to memorize them,

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.840
this would be a good thing to memorize.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:54.180
Now what's the topic that as he bows down?

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.947
By the way, I'm going to
recite the lines for you.

00:08:56.947 --> 00:08:58.363
,GANG GIS RTEN CING 'BREL BAR 'BYUNG,

00:08:58.363 --> 00:09:00.412
,'GAG PA MED PA SKYE MED PA,

00:09:00.412 --> 00:09:02.254
,CHAD PA MED PA RTAG MED PA,

00:09:02.254 --> 00:09:04.712
,'ONG BA MED PA 'GRO MED PA,

00:09:04.712 --> 00:09:06.879
,THA DAD DON MIN DON GCIG MIN,

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.253
,SPROS PA NYER ZHI ZHI BSTAN PA,

00:09:09.253 --> 00:09:11.279
,RDZOGS PA'I SANGS RGYAS SMRA RNAMS KYI,

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:14.104
,DAM PA DE LA PHYAG 'TSAL LO,,

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.620
Okay, he bows down to the Buddha.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.213
And it's very, very interesting.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.090
He starts out this first verse with GANG.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.440
And in Sanskrit it's yah.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.460
And it's kind of famous
way to start a verse,

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.730
and it's kind of a guessing game.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.960
He goes, "I'm thinking of somebody",

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.630
and then he describes the person,

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.282
and then you're supposed
to guess who's this person.

00:09:55.282 --> 00:09:57.800
You see, that's a
traditional Sanskrit stotra,

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:02.800
or a praise of somebody,
singing someone's praises.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.910
I'm thinking of the most
beautiful lady in the world.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.720
Some blonde hair, and
brown eyes, and so sweet.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:11.910
Guess who I'm talking about?

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:15.180
Then you're supposed to
guess who he's talking about.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:20.180
So these two verses,
two shlokas in Sanskrit,

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.930
they are the most famous verses,

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.930
probably, about emptiness,
of ever, of ever.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:31.460
And let's go through the meaning of them.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.330
Let's talk about... let's
break down the meaning

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:38.623
of the Sanskrit,sorry, the Tibetan.

00:10:38.623 --> 00:10:40.973
We can do the Sanskrit sometime.

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:43.520
GANG GIS RTEN CING 'BREL BAR 'BYUNG

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.590
I'm thinking of somebody who was teaching

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:51.590
about the idea that things
happen from other things.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.750
If this happens, that happens.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:00.560
If the seed is there and it
gets wet, it will grow a tree.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.720
And if this mantra, if this
Medicine Buddha mantra is here

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.560
and it's done correctly,
then it could cure disease,

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.990
or it could bring
someone to enlightenment.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:12.207
You see?

00:11:12.207 --> 00:11:17.207
So he's thinking somebody taught
us how things really work,

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.270
because the whole topic of this book

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:23.150
is that things don't
work the way you think.

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.170
Things don't work the
way you think, right?

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:30.205
And I don't know, I have a garden.

00:11:30.205 --> 00:11:32.980
It's time to plant some flowers.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.390
I put the seeds in the ground.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.510
I water them.

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:39.063
I put biochar on all my plants.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.680
And then sometimes they grow

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.387
and then sometimes they don't grow at all.

00:11:47.723 --> 00:11:51.030
Recently I planted three peach trees

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:54.860
and two of them are in very good soil.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.990
They have good water, no stones.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.790
They didn't grow so well.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.140
One of them is in rocky soil.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.320
It's out in the middle of... you know,

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.630
it shouldn't grow, but that one grew.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.580
So it means that something's going on.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:13.580
It means that the things we
think are causes are not causes,

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:17.720
and things we don't think
are causes are really causes.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:22.720
And I will say, things
that we think cause things,

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:27.470
don't cause things, sorry, and things

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:32.117
that we didn't think cause
things do cause things.

00:12:32.117 --> 00:12:34.360
GANG GIS RTEN CING 'BREL BAR 'BYUNG

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.820
Then he goes into something called,

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:39.730
and it's very important for our review:

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.970
"The eight impossibles",
eight different impossibles.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.370
Eight things are impossible.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.630
For example, a seed cannot grow a tree.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.680
That's impossible.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.030
A mantra cannot heal a disease.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:54.210
That's impossible.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.300
Not possible.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:13:00.690
There are three, sorry, there
are eight kinds of impossible.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:04.710
And in his first bowing
down to the Buddha,

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.650
Arya Nargajuna gives
us the us those eight.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:07.790
So here they are:

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:11.200
'GAG PA MED PA, nothing
stops the way you think.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:15.977
The disease doesn't stop from
the mantra, the way you think.

00:13:15.977 --> 00:13:18.890
SKYE MED PA, your understanding

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.439
from saying the mantra, it
doesn't come the way you think.

00:13:23.439 --> 00:13:26.670
CHAD PA MED PA RTAG MED
PA, things don't stop.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:31.340
Things aren't cut off and
things don't continue over time

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:34.010
in the way you think they do.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:37.440
'ONG BA MED PA 'GRO MED
PA, even when you go

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:40.470
to sit down on your meditation cushion

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.220
and then you do your mantras and you get

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:44.320
up from your meditation cushion,

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:47.670
the way you sit on the
cushion and the way you

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:51.610
get up off the cushion to do
your Medicine Buddha mantras,

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:54.330
even that's not what
you think is going on.

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:58.790
If you don't even know
how you're sitting down,

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:02.200
how are you going to understand
how to do the mantras?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.440
Much more complicated.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:08.200
Even when you put your
bottom on the cushion,

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.380
you don't really know what's happening.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:13.690
And so if you sit on the
cushion and do mantras

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:15.320
how you are going to
know what's happening?

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:19.407
So you have to understand
the emptiness of the mantra,

00:14:19.407 --> 00:14:21.900
the emptiness of the Medicine Buddha,

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.900
and the emptiness of sitting
down and standing up.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:29.400
'ONG BA MED PA 'GRO MED PA,
THA DAD DON MIN DON GCIG MIN,

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.260
Things are not separate from each other.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:34.763
I'm not separate from
the camera right now.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:40.500
But I'm also not not separate.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:45.264
I'm not separate, but
I'm not not separate.

00:14:45.264 --> 00:14:47.020
What does that mean?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.070
Is the seed separate from the tree?

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:53.410
Is the mantra of Medicine Buddha separate

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.020
from curing disease, or
reaching enlightenment?

00:14:57.020 --> 00:15:00.060
Are they separate, or
are they the same thing?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.750
If they're separate, do they touch?

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:04.750
If they're the same thing, then why do you

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.669
have to do the mantra, because
it's already enlightenment?

00:15:07.669 --> 00:15:10.133
So that's a big question.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.480
SPROS PA NYER ZHI ZHI BSTAN PA

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.800
SPROS PA here means we tend

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:20.800
to project our wrong
ideas onto other people.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:24.880
The big example is the
husband in the kitchen.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.520
We come home from a hard day at work.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:32.023
We walk in the kitchen peacefully.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.410
We don't want to fight. And then suddenly

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:39.500
the husband starts acting
strange, and saying things.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.200
Then you're like, "Wow,
I didn't do anything,

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.380
"and he seems unhappy at me today,

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.470
"but I didn't do anything".

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:51.350
So that's an example of SPROS PA.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:56.350
SPROS PA means you're making up a story

00:15:58.300 --> 00:15:59.800
about your husband,

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.170
that you didn't do anything.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.240
That's called SPROS PA.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:05.080
A story that you made
up about your husband.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.070
The truth is, as you know the story,

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.100
you yelled at your kids last week, right?

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.040
You did something last week.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.600
But you made up a story
about your husband.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.857
That's called SPROS PA.

00:16:15.857 --> 00:16:20.857
SPROS PA NYER ZHI ZHI BSTAN PA
Nargajuna says, "This person

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.183
that I'm thinking of", who
he hasn't identified yet,

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:28.720
"I'm thinking of a
person who taught us how

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.960
"to shut down those fake stories

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.370
"about your husband, or your wife."

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.250
There's something who taught us shanti,

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:40.110
how to get to the peace

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:43.830
which is shutting down your stupid stories

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:46.383
about your husband.

00:16:46.383 --> 00:16:48.110
RDZOGS PA'I SANGS RGYAS, and then finally,

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.385
in the second half of the second verse,

00:16:50.385 --> 00:16:53.010
he says, "Guess what?
I'll tell you who it was."

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:57.030
RDZOGS PA'I SANGS RGYAS
SMRA RNAMS KYI DAM PA

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.040
the totally enlightened Buddha,

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.560
who is the highest of all teachers.

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:03.120
That's who it was.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.260
That's who it was who taught us

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.890
how seeds really make trees,

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:10.310
who taught us why husbands are yelling,

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:13.920
who taught us why Medicine
Buddha mantras work.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:18.690
This is the - dan-da-da-da! -
the fully enlightened Buddha,

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:21.717
the greatest of teachers,
SMRA RNAMS KYI DAM PA.

00:17:21.717 --> 00:17:24.803
And then DE LA PHYAG 'TSAL LO
I bow down to this teacher.

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:30.750
The English translation and
English order will be reversed.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.740
I bow down to that highest of teachers,

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.910
to the fully enlightened
one who teaches us

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.210
to reach that peace, where our fantasies

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:44.290
about how things exist
are put to a final rest.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:47.180
I bow down to the one who taught us

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.440
that things happen in dependence:

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:54.180
nothing ends, nothing
begins, nothing stops,

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.170
but nothing ever lasts forever,

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:58.810
nothing comes and nothing goes.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:02.933
No two things are different,
nor are any two the same.

00:18:04.019 --> 00:18:07.560
So there's the beginning of the book.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.670
If you're going to die today,

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.950
at least you heard the most
important part of the book.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.100
That's the first verse.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:17.720
And really, if you have
time, you should memorize it

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.670
in your own language maybe.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.300
And by the way, it doesn't
matter what language it is.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.070
The important thing is to learn it

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:25.773
and have it singing in your head.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:31.599
All right. Then let's go

00:18:31.599 --> 00:18:32.520
through those eight impossibles quickly.

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.463
Here's the first idim.
Here's the first picture.

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.370
Nothing can end.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.418
If you do do Medicine Buddha mantras,

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:47.350
don't expect your physical problems,

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:52.080
or those of your loved ones
to end, because nothing ends.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.690
It's not possible for something

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.930
to end because you did mantras.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:59.500
Now that sounds very negative.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.737
It sounds like Geshe-la's telling you

00:19:01.737 --> 00:19:04.320
just forget doing mantras. It's not that.

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:07.927
The way you think the
mantra works is wrong.

00:19:07.927 --> 00:19:11.390
And if the way you think
about the mantra, how it works

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:15.460
is wrong, it will affect
how the mantra works.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.810
Will the mantra work on its own?

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:19.780
To some extent the mantra has a power.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:23.890
But if you understand how it
works, it will really work.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:27.830
So first of all, and
it's very interesting,

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:30.510
there's a big debate.

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:34.020
Nargajuna doesn't say nothing
starts and nothing stops.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:37.940
He says nothing stops and nothing starts.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.140
And there's a big argument
why he starts with stopping,

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.520
instead of starting with starting.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:46.850
You guys have to think about it.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:51.113
For some reason, he's in
the mood of negatives.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:55.640
You got the clue? It's emptiness.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:57.320
Something's not there.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.660
Stop thinking like that

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.730
and then you can start
thinking like that, okay?

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:05.730
Then he talks about how things can begin

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:10.760
and like that, how they
couldn't last forever,

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:13.093
how they could come, how they could go.

00:20:13.093 --> 00:20:16.330
That's pretty much a summary

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:17.940
of the first chapter.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:22.510
And again to teach this book carefully

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:24.913
would take about 20 years.

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:30.430
So we're going to try to jump

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:33.923
across the river on
stones of the main ideas.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:36.321
Second chapter is called

00:20:36.321 --> 00:20:38.737
"An Investigation of Going and Coming",

00:20:38.737 --> 00:20:41.473
'GRO 'ONG GI BRTAG PA in Tibetan.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:47.100
And the theme is: look, if there's no me

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:53.660
and there's no mine, then
who comes into this life

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:55.090
and who goes to the next life?

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:58.730
If there's no me, then
who came into this life

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.340
and who goes out in this life?

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:01.760
Who goes to the next life?

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.780
So the second chapter is an investigation

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:08.130
of if there's... According
to the opening lines,

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:10.230
there's no coming, there's no going.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:12.500
Well then, who comes into this life

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.830
and who goes out of this life?

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.140
And as you may remember, and by the way,

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:22.870
I encourage you to go back and
look at the earlier segments

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:24.553
on The Knowledge Base, probably?

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:30.330
If you weren't there for
the first eight chapters,

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:33.960
then I really encourage
you to look at the videos

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:38.050
for the first eight chapters
because this book is deep.

00:21:38.050 --> 00:21:41.240
And if you don't have a good foundation

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:42.410
in the earlier chapters,

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.620
you're going to have trouble
in the later chapters.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:47.300
You're going to have trouble
in the first chapters

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:48.600
with all the preparation,

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:53.560
but you're going to have more
trouble if you don't prepare.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:58.560
And those of you will remember
that we were talking about,

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:02.210
the whole discussion in
chapter two was based

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:04.343
on three parts of a path.

00:22:05.227 --> 00:22:09.653
And we'll show a picture
here of walking, right?

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:13.430
Walking along a path.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:17.900
And there's this idea that
there's a part of the path

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:20.690
that you already walked on,

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:23.903
and there's a part of the path
that you're going to walk on,

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:26.790
and then there's a part of the path

00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:30.563
between those two where
you are stepping now.

00:22:32.178 --> 00:22:36.600
So how long is the part
you already walked on

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:40.090
and how long is the part
you're going to walk on,

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:44.210
and how big is the part
you're walking on now?

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:47.853
Maybe it's so thin that it's not there.

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:51.770
Where's the line between
where you already step

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:54.980
and where you're going to step?

00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:56.123
How big is that line?

00:22:57.830 --> 00:22:59.720
And you're like, "Geshe-la, who cares?"

00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:01.561
Right? who cares?

00:23:01.561 --> 00:23:03.220
Well, you're going to to be doing mantras

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:04.470
for Medicine Buddha, right?

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:08.850
You're going to start the
mantra: om, you guys say, om.

00:23:08.850 --> 00:23:11.460
And then you're going to say
sva ha or something at the end.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.930
And you said there's going
to be a start to the mantra,

00:23:14.930 --> 00:23:17.860
a part of the mantra you already said,

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:20.900
and there's a part of the
mantra you didn't say yet,

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:23.553
and there's a part of the
mantra that you're saying now,

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.821
but it can't exist without
the start of the mantra

00:23:28.821 --> 00:23:29.654
and the end of the mantra.

00:23:29.654 --> 00:23:31.663
But the start of the
mantra stopped already,

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.980
and the end of the mantra hasn't come yet.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:38.360
If the mantra that
you're saying is halfway

00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:41.820
between those two, and
one of them doesn't exist

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:43.780
or both of them don't exist,

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:46.970
well, how can you be saying a mantra?

00:23:46.970 --> 00:23:48.630
So that was chapter two.

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:51.460
If you can not answer
that question right now,

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:54.330
go study chapter two again.

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:56.460
Let's look at chapter three.

00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:59.440
And this was our... by the way,

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:02.010
the first two chapters we covered

00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:06.270
in the first Nargajuna
course. And then now

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:10.310
here's the second Nargajuna
course that we did.

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.300
Then after that we're
going to start this course,

00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:15.310
which is course number three.

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:17.430
And my plan is five years.

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:21.790
We can get through this
great, extraordinary book

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:26.410
in five years. We will do

00:24:26.410 --> 00:24:31.410
about 15 classes each year.

00:24:31.930 --> 00:24:36.270
So I think in about 75 classes
we can finish the book,

00:24:36.270 --> 00:24:38.310
something like that.

00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:41.610
If you have time, you should go learn it.

00:24:41.610 --> 00:24:43.710
We could go study Chandrakirti,

00:24:43.710 --> 00:24:45.610
and then we could go study Tsongkapa.

00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:48.400
You know, that would be a long story.

00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:53.030
But these five years of five courses

00:24:53.030 --> 00:24:57.113
should give you a deep
understanding of emptiness.

00:24:57.113 --> 00:24:59.160
And then you take that understanding

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.810
and you use it for your
Medicine Buddha practice

00:25:01.810 --> 00:25:04.270
and you use it for your life.

00:25:04.270 --> 00:25:09.270
Chapter three was an
investigation of the powers.

00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:13.860
And this power means...
"Indriya" means your eye, ear

00:25:13.860 --> 00:25:18.140
and nose, tongue, body, your sense powers,

00:25:18.140 --> 00:25:21.853
mainly your sense powers and
also other powers of your mind.

00:25:23.060 --> 00:25:27.030
This is one of three chapters:

00:25:27.030 --> 00:25:30.060
chapter three, chapter four, chapter five.

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:34.740
They present topics
that Lord Buddha talked

00:25:34.740 --> 00:25:37.900
about in the early stage of his teaching,

00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:39.690
in the first turning of the wheel,

00:25:39.690 --> 00:25:42.450
like Abhidharma, basic Abhidharma.

00:25:42.450 --> 00:25:47.420
And it's famous that in his early years,

00:25:47.420 --> 00:25:49.390
Buddha didn't deny anything.

00:25:49.390 --> 00:25:52.010
He just said, let's
learn about the powers.

00:25:52.010 --> 00:25:53.980
Let's learn about the elements.

00:25:53.980 --> 00:25:56.730
Let's learn about the
five parts of a person.

00:25:56.730 --> 00:25:59.740
And nowhere did he say they don't exist.

00:25:59.740 --> 00:26:01.750
That was in the second
turning of the wheel.

00:26:01.750 --> 00:26:03.850
So remember the three
turnings of the wheel.

00:26:03.850 --> 00:26:05.583
First turning of the wheel:

00:26:05.583 --> 00:26:07.480
look, you've got the sense powers,

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:11.703
mental powers, you've got
these five parts of a person.

00:26:12.540 --> 00:26:15.470
And you have these other parts

00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:17.120
of you called the elements, right?

00:26:17.120 --> 00:26:18.790
The chemicals that make you up,

00:26:18.790 --> 00:26:22.020
or the elemental forces that make you up.

00:26:22.020 --> 00:26:23.460
And nowhere in the first turning

00:26:23.460 --> 00:26:28.460
of the wheel did Lord Buddha
obviously say they didn't exist

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:31.240
or they were empty or something like that.

00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:33.963
So the next three chapters
- three, four and five -

00:26:34.900 --> 00:26:37.020
we're going to bring up three topics

00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:40.810
that Lord Buddha covered
early in his career

00:26:40.810 --> 00:26:43.860
in the days when he wasn't
talking about emptiness.

00:26:43.860 --> 00:26:46.210
Then suddenly I think he
fell down and he hit his head

00:26:46.210 --> 00:26:49.091
on a brick, and he starts saying

00:26:49.091 --> 00:26:50.824
The Heart Sutra and The
Diamond Cutter Sutra.

00:26:50.824 --> 00:26:52.340
Nothing exists,

00:26:52.340 --> 00:26:56.150
and then all the students got confused.

00:26:56.150 --> 00:26:59.130
And the whole third turning
of the wheel was the students,

00:26:59.130 --> 00:27:02.420
confused students, asking
him what the heck's going on.

00:27:02.420 --> 00:27:04.810
Did you hit your head or something?

00:27:04.810 --> 00:27:09.810
So the next three chapters
treat basic Buddhist topics,

00:27:11.390 --> 00:27:14.990
which I thought were safe,
but they're not safe.

00:27:14.990 --> 00:27:16.960
They're also all messed up.

00:27:16.960 --> 00:27:18.540
They're also crazy.

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:21.961
And that's a theme of Nargajuna.

00:27:21.961 --> 00:27:25.570
Nargajuna wants you to understand

00:27:25.570 --> 00:27:29.640
that there's a basic problem
with how you see the world.

00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:34.010
There's something going on
that you don't understand.

00:27:34.010 --> 00:27:35.170
Why?

00:27:35.170 --> 00:27:40.170
You spend 30, 40, 50 years
trying to make your life work:

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:43.860
make money, have relationships,
have good health,

00:27:43.860 --> 00:27:45.150
be a happy person.

00:27:45.150 --> 00:27:47.550
You struggle, struggle, struggle.

00:27:47.550 --> 00:27:49.490
And then somehow it just doesn't work.

00:27:49.490 --> 00:27:51.930
Didn't you notice yet?

00:27:51.930 --> 00:27:53.620
Didn't you notice yet?

00:27:53.620 --> 00:27:55.100
People do yoga.

00:27:55.100 --> 00:27:57.710
I have a friend he does yoga all the time.

00:27:57.710 --> 00:27:59.733
They're having a hip operation soon,

00:28:00.846 --> 00:28:03.670
because the yoga messed up their hips.

00:28:03.670 --> 00:28:06.040
And then, wait a minute,
the yoga was supposed

00:28:06.040 --> 00:28:07.070
to make me healthy.

00:28:07.070 --> 00:28:10.530
Yeah, I know, but it
doesn't work like that.

00:28:10.530 --> 00:28:12.650
The mantra made me nervous.

00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:14.123
Yeah, it happens.

00:28:15.270 --> 00:28:16.570
Well, why doesn't it work?

00:28:16.570 --> 00:28:19.780
Well, that's not how...
Mantra doesn't work by itself.

00:28:19.780 --> 00:28:21.560
Mantra works because of something else.

00:28:21.560 --> 00:28:26.560
So we're going to take the
basic, basic facts of life.

00:28:28.980 --> 00:28:32.420
And Nargajuna says,
look, something's wrong.

00:28:32.420 --> 00:28:34.840
People who exercise every day

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:36.710
go get hip surgeries.

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:39.540
And then there's people who
don't exercise every day,

00:28:39.540 --> 00:28:44.540
like Pachi, who look great!
How does that work out?

00:28:45.426 --> 00:28:47.284
What is that?

00:28:48.120 --> 00:28:51.720
So we're trying to look into these.

00:28:51.720 --> 00:28:54.430
Fishy. Something's fishy.

00:28:54.430 --> 00:28:58.340
In American English,
fishy means smells bad.

00:28:58.340 --> 00:29:02.800
And it means something's going on.

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:07.580
Like I just bought a cafe. Not just.

00:29:07.580 --> 00:29:09.920
I bought a cafe almost two years ago.

00:29:09.920 --> 00:29:13.870
And I'm supposed to go
down to the county office,

00:29:13.870 --> 00:29:16.530
the government, local
tiny government office.

00:29:16.530 --> 00:29:18.130
I'm supposed to ask, "Please,

00:29:18.130 --> 00:29:20.580
I want to add a new door on the bathroom."

00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:23.880
And then the guy signs it and
says, "Okay, add a new door."

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:27.770
And it's taking me almost
two years to get him

00:29:27.770 --> 00:29:31.010
to sign the paper for the new door.

00:29:31.010 --> 00:29:33.810
And then I start thinking,
something's fishy, you know.

00:29:33.810 --> 00:29:37.070
Maybe this other restaurant
guy is paying him not

00:29:37.070 --> 00:29:41.210
to give me a license. Or
maybe he wants a bribe,

00:29:41.210 --> 00:29:42.940
I don't know what's going on.

00:29:42.940 --> 00:29:44.530
And we say, something's fishy.

00:29:44.530 --> 00:29:48.290
Something's fishy means
something weird is going on.

00:29:48.290 --> 00:29:52.090
And Nargajuna says, everything's fishy.

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:54.260
Again, everything about
everything is fishy.

00:29:54.260 --> 00:29:58.030
Didn't you notice that
the people who do yoga

00:29:58.030 --> 00:29:59.250
go get hip operations.

00:29:59.250 --> 00:30:01.820
And the people who eat all day, like Tim,

00:30:01.820 --> 00:30:04.210
look great and thin.

00:30:04.210 --> 00:30:06.513
Isn't there something going on here?

00:30:07.510 --> 00:30:09.660
Do you think, maybe?

00:30:09.660 --> 00:30:13.410
So Nargarjuna's methodology is to say,

00:30:13.410 --> 00:30:15.170
look, something's weird.

00:30:15.170 --> 00:30:17.800
Something doesn't work the
way you thought it worked.

00:30:17.800 --> 00:30:20.750
Some people eat all day
and they look great.

00:30:20.750 --> 00:30:25.750
Some people eat like
carrots all day, once a day,

00:30:27.080 --> 00:30:29.500
and then they got this
COVID tummy to fight with.

00:30:29.500 --> 00:30:34.500
I don't know. Something's
fishy, all right?

00:30:35.020 --> 00:30:39.320
So chapter three, which we already covered

00:30:40.479 --> 00:30:45.479
and it's talking about how
do the sense powers work.

00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:49.560
Which came first, the chicken or the egg?

00:30:49.560 --> 00:30:52.860
Which came first, the
eyeball, or colors and shapes?

00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:57.240
And there's a big discrepancy,.
Something's fishy.

00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:59.433
Nargajuna says, look, something's fishy.

00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:03.670
Something's fishy about the
idea that there's a bottle

00:31:03.670 --> 00:31:07.190
of orange liquid and
your eye. Geshe-la's eye

00:31:07.190 --> 00:31:09.720
is already sitting on the couch

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:12.840
and then Geshe-la's
eye looks at the orange

00:31:12.840 --> 00:31:14.990
and something's not right.

00:31:14.990 --> 00:31:18.500
Something's wrong about Geshe-la's seeing.

00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:23.500
And by the way, here we
go, if Geshe-la's eye came

00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:29.810
before the orange juice, then
we couldn't call it an eye,

00:31:30.600 --> 00:31:33.860
because it's not looking
at anything, okay?

00:31:33.860 --> 00:31:38.440
It's not an eye until
it looks at something.

00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:42.100
So you can't say Geshe-la
was sitting on the couch

00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:45.580
with his eyes and he turned
the eyes to the orange juice

00:31:45.580 --> 00:31:46.970
and then he saw the orange juice.

00:31:46.970 --> 00:31:50.100
Geshe-la's eyes were working

00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:51.720
before the orange juice was there.

00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:53.700
You can't say that. Why?

00:31:53.700 --> 00:31:56.710
It's not an eye to elicit something.

00:31:58.070 --> 00:32:00.550
If it's an eye before
it looks at something,

00:32:00.550 --> 00:32:02.143
then your nose is also an eye,

00:32:02.990 --> 00:32:05.940
because it doesn't look
at something either.

00:32:05.940 --> 00:32:07.650
Okay, it just doesn't make sense.

00:32:07.650 --> 00:32:08.550
I'll say it again.

00:32:09.429 --> 00:32:12.210
And Nargajuna, you got
to say it like 10 times.

00:32:12.210 --> 00:32:15.320
Was Geshe-la's eye on the couch

00:32:15.320 --> 00:32:18.143
before he looked at the orange color?

00:32:19.020 --> 00:32:20.920
And Nargajuna says, no, are you crazy?

00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:22.930
And you say, no, no, I was on the couch

00:32:22.930 --> 00:32:24.140
and then I picked up the orange.

00:32:24.140 --> 00:32:27.010
Come on, you're saying your eye was an eye

00:32:27.010 --> 00:32:28.670
before you held up the orange?

00:32:28.670 --> 00:32:32.120
Yeah, the eye was waiting
and then the orange came.

00:32:32.120 --> 00:32:34.000
Yeah, well what's an eye?

00:32:34.000 --> 00:32:35.830
An eye is something that sees things.

00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:37.047
But it wasn't seeing anything

00:32:37.047 --> 00:32:38.460
before you picked up an orange though.

00:32:38.460 --> 00:32:40.596
So it wasn't an eye, don't you get it?

00:32:44.496 --> 00:32:45.800
But then after you picked up the orange,

00:32:45.800 --> 00:32:48.120
the eye's already gone.

00:32:48.120 --> 00:32:52.848
Duh, the orange came,
there must've been an eye

00:32:52.848 --> 00:32:54.580
after you saw the orange

00:32:54.580 --> 00:32:56.733
the eye was already,
let's put it this way:

00:32:58.340 --> 00:33:00.440
The orange made the eye a seer.

00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:03.030
So the orange came first.

00:33:03.030 --> 00:33:06.000
The orange came first,
then the eye came later.

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:10.458
Yeah, but if the eye wasn't
there yet, who saw the orange?

00:33:10.458 --> 00:33:12.310
Nargajuna says, don't you get it?

00:33:12.310 --> 00:33:14.070
Something weird is going on.

00:33:14.070 --> 00:33:16.630
All those yoga guys are
getting hip operations.

00:33:16.630 --> 00:33:20.897
All those people doing Medicine
Buddha mantras all day,

00:33:20.897 --> 00:33:22.640
they're also getting sick.

00:33:22.640 --> 00:33:24.440
What's going on?

00:33:24.440 --> 00:33:27.150
And he's asking us to think about it,

00:33:27.150 --> 00:33:28.170
starting with your eye.

00:33:28.170 --> 00:33:33.170
Chapter four, I mean one of
the first great teachings

00:33:34.650 --> 00:33:36.780
of the Buddha is the
five parts of a person,

00:33:36.780 --> 00:33:38.470
the five heaps. Right?

00:33:38.470 --> 00:33:42.230
So there's five parts to you: your body,

00:33:42.230 --> 00:33:46.270
your capacity of feeling, your
capacity of discrimination,

00:33:46.270 --> 00:33:49.640
all the other parts about
you, all the other stuff.

00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:52.210
All the other parts of Tim.

00:33:52.210 --> 00:33:55.636
That's like me, I try not to
sneeze too when I'm sleeping,

00:33:55.636 --> 00:33:56.593
so V doesn't get wake up.

00:33:58.160 --> 00:34:03.160
Okay anyway. And fifthly, your
mind, you're raw awareness.

00:34:03.320 --> 00:34:07.823
So look, Buddha never said,
Nargajuna, that they were empty.

00:34:08.800 --> 00:34:10.380
sS what's that all about?

00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:12.590
You say they're empty.

00:34:12.590 --> 00:34:16.360
And then Nargajuna says, look,
if I discuss the five heaps,

00:34:16.360 --> 00:34:20.010
the five parts to you,
it would take a year.

00:34:20.010 --> 00:34:22.450
Let's just talk about
your physical body, okay?

00:34:22.450 --> 00:34:25.873
First part. Pachi's arm, Pachi's ear,

00:34:26.714 --> 00:34:27.760
you know, Rebecca's nose.

00:34:27.760 --> 00:34:30.290
Let's talk about your physical.

00:34:30.290 --> 00:34:33.347
In the fourth chapter, which is called,

00:34:33.347 --> 00:34:36.130
"An Investigation of the
Five Parts of a Person",

00:34:36.130 --> 00:34:39.740
he doesn't bother
investigating four of them.

00:34:39.740 --> 00:34:43.420
He says, let's get your body straight

00:34:43.420 --> 00:34:46.200
and then we can talk about the rest.

00:34:46.200 --> 00:34:50.150
We got this lady looking at her arm.

00:34:50.150 --> 00:34:52.920
The causes that made her arm,

00:34:52.920 --> 00:34:56.843
which you can say is skin
or chemicals in the skin,

00:34:58.380 --> 00:35:01.283
they weren't causes
until the arm was there.

00:35:02.230 --> 00:35:04.910
You can't call something
a cause until the result.

00:35:04.910 --> 00:35:07.920
When you see a result, you
can say something is a cause.

00:35:07.920 --> 00:35:09.350
Oh, look, somebody got better.

00:35:09.350 --> 00:35:11.146
What was the cause?

00:35:11.146 --> 00:35:13.850
They were doing mantras,
Medicine Buddha mantras.

00:35:13.850 --> 00:35:18.440
But you can't talk about the
causes of good health as causes

00:35:21.980 --> 00:35:23.530
until the good health comes.

00:35:23.530 --> 00:35:26.683
Therefore they must be the same time.

00:35:29.570 --> 00:35:31.790
If you do a mantra to stop cancer,

00:35:31.790 --> 00:35:34.300
then before you finish the first mantra,

00:35:34.300 --> 00:35:38.653
the cancer should go away,
if things work like that.

00:35:39.842 --> 00:35:43.467
So he's said, look, try
to understand the things

00:35:45.010 --> 00:35:48.760
that made your arm didn't make your arm,

00:35:48.760 --> 00:35:52.170
because it's not until the arm is there

00:35:52.170 --> 00:35:55.020
that you can say they were causes.

00:35:55.020 --> 00:35:58.512
Until the result comes you
can't call something a cause.

00:35:58.512 --> 00:36:01.220
Until smoke comes, you can't
say there's a fire there.

00:36:01.220 --> 00:36:02.530
You can't.

00:36:02.530 --> 00:36:04.490
The smoke indicates the fire.

00:36:04.490 --> 00:36:07.323
The arm indicates the causes of the arm.

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:14.290
Until the arm is created by
the chemicals in the skin,

00:36:14.670 --> 00:36:19.320
you can't call the chemicals
in the skin causes of the arm,

00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:20.953
because there's no arm yet.

00:36:21.920 --> 00:36:25.150
And if the arm's not there
yet, the result's not there.

00:36:25.150 --> 00:36:26.690
If the result's not there yet,

00:36:26.690 --> 00:36:29.010
you can't call anything
causes of the result,

00:36:29.010 --> 00:36:32.540
because the result
doesn't have causes yet.

00:36:32.540 --> 00:36:34.450
So that's the fourth chapter.

00:36:34.450 --> 00:36:39.400
If you feel confused, you're
in the right place, okay?

00:36:39.400 --> 00:36:41.560
If you're starting to doubt your mantras,

00:36:41.560 --> 00:36:43.150
you're in the right place.

00:36:43.150 --> 00:36:45.320
You should doubt your mantras.

00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:48.460
Come on, didn't you notice
not everyone who says,

00:36:48.460 --> 00:36:51.360
Medicine Buddha mantras have
been said for 2000 years.

00:36:51.360 --> 00:36:55.470
All those people died. Duh.

00:36:55.470 --> 00:36:58.028
Then there must be something else going on

00:36:58.028 --> 00:37:00.290
and there must be something
else that makes the mantra work.

00:37:00.290 --> 00:37:04.358
By the way, not all those people died,

00:37:04.358 --> 00:37:06.080
probably a lot of them didn't
die, but we don't see it.

00:37:06.080 --> 00:37:07.620
We can't see it.

00:37:07.620 --> 00:37:09.170
All right, Chapter number five.

00:37:10.207 --> 00:37:12.247
"An Investigation of the Elements".

00:37:14.337 --> 00:37:16.540
"An Investigation of the Elements".

00:37:16.540 --> 00:37:18.800
And these are SA, CHU, ME, RLUNG,

00:37:18.800 --> 00:37:22.313
you know, earth, water, fire, wind.

00:37:23.260 --> 00:37:26.700
And you know, it's very common to say,

00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:30.200
oh, here's fire by the way.

00:37:30.200 --> 00:37:34.490
There's fire in her hands
that help create her hands.

00:37:34.490 --> 00:37:37.511
And then she's also feeling the fire.

00:37:38.360 --> 00:37:42.370
And these are not some
stupid Ayurvedic thing

00:37:42.370 --> 00:37:44.090
from 2000 years ago.

00:37:44.090 --> 00:37:45.403
It's not like that.

00:37:46.510 --> 00:37:51.510
For example, nowadays in physics,
we would call it inertia,

00:37:52.350 --> 00:37:55.640
or gravity, or bonding forces.

00:37:55.640 --> 00:37:58.363
These are the elemental forces.

00:37:59.740 --> 00:38:02.250
It's not that Nargajuna
thought there was some fire

00:38:02.250 --> 00:38:03.367
inside your arm or something like that.

00:38:03.367 --> 00:38:08.100
And by the way, Nargajuna
was a master of the elements.

00:38:08.100 --> 00:38:10.170
He was an Alchemist.

00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:11.770
He was famous for making gold.

00:38:11.770 --> 00:38:16.000
He got in trouble for making
gold, which is a long story.

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.910
He knew how chemicals work.

00:38:18.910 --> 00:38:20.940
He knew how the elements work.

00:38:20.940 --> 00:38:24.583
And he knew the basic forces of physics,

00:38:27.126 --> 00:38:29.130
the forces that bond things together,

00:38:29.130 --> 00:38:31.030
the forces that tear things apart.

00:38:31.030 --> 00:38:35.713
He understood them, gravity and
inertia, he understood them.

00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:41.540
So if there are certain forces

00:38:41.540 --> 00:38:46.367
that are underneath
everything, if this bottle cap

00:38:47.550 --> 00:38:52.200
has some fire in it, if
it has some temperature,

00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:54.280
it's not an absolute zero, right?

00:38:54.280 --> 00:38:55.920
So it has some temperature.

00:38:55.920 --> 00:38:57.640
It also has some fluidity.

00:38:57.640 --> 00:38:59.820
It can stretch a little bit.

00:38:59.820 --> 00:39:00.653
It has water.

00:39:00.653 --> 00:39:01.840
It has fire.

00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:06.840
If it has those things,
well, which came first?

00:39:06.850 --> 00:39:08.620
And by the way, it's here

00:39:08.620 --> 00:39:11.500
in the "Investigation of the Elements",

00:39:11.500 --> 00:39:16.500
that Nargajuna really gets
into: How do you define things?

00:39:18.380 --> 00:39:21.650
How do you decide something is a fire?

00:39:21.650 --> 00:39:24.500
Well, what's your definition of fire?

00:39:24.500 --> 00:39:29.500
I say fire is an energy that causes heat

00:39:29.530 --> 00:39:31.520
and is typified by burning.

00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:35.370
I say fire is an energy that causes heat

00:39:36.290 --> 00:39:38.810
and it's typified by
the burning of things.

00:39:38.810 --> 00:39:39.940
That's what I say.

00:39:39.940 --> 00:39:42.273
That's a definition of fire.

00:39:43.920 --> 00:39:44.753
What?

00:39:44.753 --> 00:39:46.440
What's the definition of fire?

00:39:46.440 --> 00:39:48.220
TSA ZHING SREG PA

00:39:48.220 --> 00:39:50.443
in Tibetan, quickly ,you
say hot and burning.

00:39:51.620 --> 00:39:54.550
Okay, so which came first, the definition

00:39:54.550 --> 00:39:56.370
or the thing you want to define?

00:39:56.370 --> 00:39:58.870
Well, the thing you want to
define has to come first,

00:39:58.870 --> 00:40:01.250
otherwise you don't know
what you're defining.

00:40:01.250 --> 00:40:05.060
I wasn't talking about bananas,
I was talking about fire.

00:40:05.060 --> 00:40:07.370
Well okay, tell me what
you want to define first.

00:40:07.370 --> 00:40:11.330
Okay, bananas, fire,
what's your definition?

00:40:11.330 --> 00:40:12.210
Hot and burning.

00:40:12.210 --> 00:40:13.380
Which came first?

00:40:13.380 --> 00:40:14.213
Fire.

00:40:14.213 --> 00:40:15.046
Which came second?

00:40:15.046 --> 00:40:15.879
Hot and burning.

00:40:15.879 --> 00:40:17.460
How can you have fire
without hot and burning?

00:40:17.460 --> 00:40:18.990
Are you crazy?

00:40:18.990 --> 00:40:21.700
Come on, the definition came first.

00:40:21.700 --> 00:40:24.793
Then the thing came, hot
and fire, hot and burning.

00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:29.695
Then you say what you're
defining: bananas.

00:40:30.840 --> 00:40:33.290
No, but Geshe-la there's no
connection between banana,

00:40:33.290 --> 00:40:34.123
and hot and burning.

00:40:34.123 --> 00:40:35.623
Well, there's no connection between fire,

00:40:35.623 --> 00:40:36.490
and hot and burning.

00:40:36.490 --> 00:40:38.270
It's just a word.

00:40:38.270 --> 00:40:43.270
So, you can't even define the things

00:40:45.030 --> 00:40:48.063
that make up the bottom
that you're sitting on.

00:40:50.330 --> 00:40:53.120
So how can you use Medicine
Buddha mantras? Come on.

00:40:53.120 --> 00:40:55.620
How are you going to use a mantra?

00:40:55.620 --> 00:40:59.090
Chapter six.

00:40:59.090 --> 00:41:01.590
Don't forget, we're trying
to review eight chapters

00:41:01.590 --> 00:41:06.590
that we had already and
really, if you try to start

00:41:07.800 --> 00:41:12.160
with me on course three of
Nargajuna at chapter nine,

00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:14.870
if you try to start there without doing

00:41:14.870 --> 00:41:17.690
the first eight chapters,

00:41:17.690 --> 00:41:20.100
you're going to get more confused.

00:41:20.100 --> 00:41:21.780
But anyway, it'll be fun.

00:41:21.780 --> 00:41:26.780
By the way, in the monastery,
confusion is a technique.

00:41:27.230 --> 00:41:29.120
Confusion is a technique.

00:41:29.120 --> 00:41:31.930
And it's recognized as a technique.

00:41:31.930 --> 00:41:34.070
The teacher will sit down, say,

00:41:34.070 --> 00:41:38.410
let's see, it's like December,

00:41:38.410 --> 00:41:41.096
let me confuse my students today.

00:41:42.680 --> 00:41:44.490
And the goal of the
teacher at that moment,

00:41:44.490 --> 00:41:47.330
is that nobody in the class
knows what's going on.

00:41:47.330 --> 00:41:49.407
And then they all get frustrated

00:41:49.407 --> 00:41:51.510
and they'll work harder, or they'll quit.

00:41:51.510 --> 00:41:54.930
So you can get rid of
the not serious students

00:41:54.930 --> 00:41:56.600
and save time.

00:41:56.600 --> 00:41:58.970
And then the serious students
are going to work harder

00:41:58.970 --> 00:42:01.030
because they're so frustrated and angry,

00:42:01.030 --> 00:42:02.900
because they don't understand anything.

00:42:02.900 --> 00:42:06.900
So confusion is a tool

00:42:06.900 --> 00:42:09.610
of the great Buddhist
teachers like Nargajuna.

00:42:09.610 --> 00:42:13.610
So if you get confused, it's on purpose..

00:42:13.610 --> 00:42:14.840
If you don't get confused,

00:42:14.840 --> 00:42:17.990
it's because I gave a good explanation.

00:42:17.990 --> 00:42:22.990
Chapter six is an investigation, pariksha,

00:42:23.340 --> 00:42:26.560
of desire and who feels the desire.

00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:29.830
Let's talk about desire
and who feels the desire.

00:42:29.830 --> 00:42:34.830
And by the way, by now
you should be smelling

00:42:34.890 --> 00:42:39.420
or feeling that there's,
in English we say, a method

00:42:39.420 --> 00:42:41.300
to Nargajuna's madness.

00:42:41.300 --> 00:42:45.385
He is not just throwing
out topics randomly.

00:42:47.446 --> 00:42:50.150
Now you're a third of
the way through this book

00:42:50.150 --> 00:42:52.050
and you should start asking yourself:

00:42:52.050 --> 00:42:55.041
What's the connection between this chapter

00:42:55.041 --> 00:42:55.874
and the last chapter?

00:42:55.874 --> 00:42:59.210
It seems like Nargajuna is
jumping around like crazy.

00:42:59.210 --> 00:43:03.430
And Geshe-la and Choney Lama
took you through the logic

00:43:03.430 --> 00:43:08.430
of all 27 chapters in the first
course. So don't complain.

00:43:08.960 --> 00:43:11.110
It's not that Nargajuna is jumping around

00:43:11.110 --> 00:43:12.220
to different topics.

00:43:12.220 --> 00:43:14.650
He has a plan.

00:43:14.650 --> 00:43:18.770
To try to see his master
plan is a great achievement.

00:43:18.770 --> 00:43:22.850
If you can get a feeling
for Nargajuna's master plan

00:43:22.850 --> 00:43:25.510
for "Wisdom", then really you're starting

00:43:25.510 --> 00:43:28.240
to understand how mantra works.

00:43:28.240 --> 00:43:32.410
So the picture here is,
I tried to find a picture

00:43:32.410 --> 00:43:34.963
of desire and this is the
one that Geshe-la has.

00:43:36.826 --> 00:43:40.700
It's a desire for churros,
or пончик (ponchik),

00:43:40.700 --> 00:43:42.936
or 油条 (yóutiáo), or doughnut.

00:43:42.936 --> 00:43:47.936
By the way, I didn't find a
good donut shop in Sedona.

00:43:48.040 --> 00:43:50.990
The best one in the universe
is in the Guadalajara Airport.

00:43:52.422 --> 00:43:55.922
Where is it? You got it?

00:43:58.190 --> 00:44:01.140
I might have to move to West Sedona.

00:44:01.140 --> 00:44:06.140
Okay, anyway, so which comes first,

00:44:06.280 --> 00:44:08.700
the desire or the person who feels it?

00:44:08.700 --> 00:44:12.190
That girl has desire for the doughnut.

00:44:12.190 --> 00:44:13.820
So who came first,

00:44:13.820 --> 00:44:15.950
the girl or the desire?

00:44:15.950 --> 00:44:17.423
She's a girl who desires.

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:22.030
So can we call her a girl who
desires before she has desire?

00:44:22.030 --> 00:44:24.441
No, you cannot.

00:44:24.441 --> 00:44:26.960
Do you have to wait until
after she has the desire

00:44:26.960 --> 00:44:28.610
to call her a girl with desire?

00:44:28.610 --> 00:44:30.320
Yeah, you do.

00:44:30.320 --> 00:44:32.460
Okay, so what made her desire?

00:44:32.460 --> 00:44:34.270
What is she desiring about?

00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:35.440
It's a doughnut.

00:44:35.440 --> 00:44:37.740
So the doughnut has to come
before the girl, right?

00:44:37.740 --> 00:44:40.130
Like before the girls born,
the doughnut should come.

00:44:40.130 --> 00:44:41.000
Why?

00:44:41.000 --> 00:44:43.630
Beause she doesn't have desire
until the doughnut is there.

00:44:43.630 --> 00:44:45.540
The doughnut has to be there first.

00:44:45.540 --> 00:44:47.800
Then you can have a girl
who wants a doughnut.

00:44:47.800 --> 00:44:49.760
So by definition, you
got to have a doughnut

00:44:49.760 --> 00:44:51.440
before you have the
girl who has the desire

00:44:51.440 --> 00:44:52.600
for the doughnut, right?

00:44:52.600 --> 00:44:53.433
Right.

00:44:56.780 --> 00:44:58.490
But the girl can't desire the doughnut

00:44:58.490 --> 00:45:00.610
until the girl's there,
so the doughnut has

00:45:00.610 --> 00:45:01.443
to come after the girl.

00:45:01.443 --> 00:45:02.680
Come on, try to get it.

00:45:02.680 --> 00:45:04.390
Try to understand what's going on.

00:45:04.390 --> 00:45:06.430
How can the girl desire a doughnut

00:45:06.430 --> 00:45:08.840
if the doughnut's not there?

00:45:08.840 --> 00:45:11.450
If the doughnut's already there,

00:45:11.450 --> 00:45:13.260
how can you have a girl desire a doughnut?

00:45:13.260 --> 00:45:14.960
And if you have a girl
who desires a doughnut,

00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:15.793
the doughnut must come first.

00:45:15.793 --> 00:45:17.583
But if the girl doesn't come first,

00:45:17.583 --> 00:45:20.020
then how can there be a
doughnut that she has desire.

00:45:20.020 --> 00:45:22.212
She should feel desire.

00:45:23.048 --> 00:45:25.900
She should have mental
afflicitons in her mind.

00:45:25.900 --> 00:45:27.150
And then she sees a doughnut

00:45:27.150 --> 00:45:28.970
and the mental affliction wakes up, right?

00:45:28.970 --> 00:45:30.163
So which came first?

00:45:31.040 --> 00:45:32.750
That's chapter six.

00:45:32.750 --> 00:45:37.217
Chapter seven, this is called

00:45:37.217 --> 00:45:42.217
"An Investigation of Starting,
Staying and Stopping".

00:45:42.620 --> 00:45:47.070
And the other guy says,
look, if things start,

00:45:47.070 --> 00:45:49.160
then they're not empty.

00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:52.070
If things stay, then they're not empty.

00:45:52.070 --> 00:45:54.840
If things stop, then they're not empty.

00:45:54.840 --> 00:45:55.673
Why?

00:45:55.673 --> 00:45:57.380
Beause they have causes.

00:45:57.380 --> 00:46:01.713
How can they say they're
empty if things don't start?

00:46:03.140 --> 00:46:05.500
If things don't start,
how can they be empty?

00:46:05.500 --> 00:46:08.040
If things start, how can they be empty?

00:46:08.040 --> 00:46:11.693
Empty means nothing about
them, but they have causes.

00:46:12.640 --> 00:46:15.820
They must have causes,
or they can't start.

00:46:15.820 --> 00:46:20.510
Causes must be inherent in
a thing for it to start,

00:46:20.510 --> 00:46:22.660
because a thing can't start without causes

00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:26.900
and especially desire cannot
start without its causes.

00:46:26.900 --> 00:46:29.520
So desire must have its causes.

00:46:29.520 --> 00:46:32.430
Therefore, desire is not empty.

00:46:32.430 --> 00:46:36.320
Nargajuna said everything
is empty, but it's not. Why?

00:46:36.320 --> 00:46:38.410
It has an inherent thing.

00:46:38.410 --> 00:46:40.263
What's the inherent thing?

00:46:40.263 --> 00:46:42.421
It doesn't happen until it has it causes

00:46:42.421 --> 00:46:45.140
that it's inherent in that thing.

00:46:45.140 --> 00:46:47.740
Desire cannot come up
unless the causes come up.

00:46:47.740 --> 00:46:50.860
That girl's not going to feel desire,

00:46:50.860 --> 00:46:53.703
I don't know, for a punch in the nose.

00:46:54.820 --> 00:46:56.500
There has to be something nice there,

00:46:56.500 --> 00:46:59.046
then you can have desire for it.

00:46:59.046 --> 00:47:01.950
There has to be a seed,
then you can have it.

00:47:01.950 --> 00:47:06.950
We're looking at a foot of a person

00:47:07.430 --> 00:47:09.580
about to run a race.

00:47:09.580 --> 00:47:12.160
And where did the race start?

00:47:12.160 --> 00:47:13.883
When did the race start?

00:47:15.570 --> 00:47:18.670
Was it when they shot the gun?

00:47:18.670 --> 00:47:21.950
Or was it the first part
of the gunshot noise,

00:47:21.950 --> 00:47:24.500
or the second part of the gunshot noise?

00:47:24.500 --> 00:47:26.720
Or was it the final part
of the gunshot noise

00:47:26.720 --> 00:47:29.780
and then the gunshot went
off, and then the people ran?

00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:31.590
So where did the race start?

00:47:31.590 --> 00:47:36.540
And you cannot find a place
where the race started.

00:47:36.540 --> 00:47:39.560
You think this guy's at the starting line,

00:47:39.560 --> 00:47:41.220
but there is no starting line.

00:47:41.220 --> 00:47:43.060
Look, his fingers on the starting line,

00:47:43.060 --> 00:47:45.200
or not on the starting line?

00:47:45.200 --> 00:47:48.430
And how far between the
finger and the starting line?

00:47:48.430 --> 00:47:51.540
What about the other side
of the starting line?

00:47:51.540 --> 00:47:53.520
Where's the starting line?

00:47:53.520 --> 00:47:57.450
And Nargajuna says, come
on, something's fishy.

00:47:57.450 --> 00:47:59.073
Chapter eight,

00:48:01.097 --> 00:48:04.510
"An Investigation of Agents and Actions".

00:48:04.510 --> 00:48:07.810
Doers and things that they do.

00:48:07.810 --> 00:48:09.630
Doers and things that they do.

00:48:09.630 --> 00:48:14.323
Let's investigate doers and
the things that they do.

00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:17.700
Well what's the big example Geshe-la?

00:48:17.700 --> 00:48:18.533
Karma.

00:48:19.540 --> 00:48:23.590
If there's no me, if there's no Michael,

00:48:23.590 --> 00:48:27.680
then who makes the karma
if there's no Michael?

00:48:27.680 --> 00:48:32.440
If there's no me and mine,
Nargajuna, then there's no karma.

00:48:32.440 --> 00:48:33.320
Why?

00:48:33.320 --> 00:48:36.100
Beause Michael has to
be there to make karma.

00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:38.190
So according to you,
what? There's no karma?

00:48:38.190 --> 00:48:39.023
Why?

00:48:39.023 --> 00:48:39.880
There's no, Michael.

00:48:39.880 --> 00:48:41.520
I didn't say there's no Michael.

00:48:41.520 --> 00:48:42.607
You did say there's no Michael.

00:48:42.607 --> 00:48:44.420
You say Michael never started.

00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:46.810
Did Michael come without starting?

00:48:46.810 --> 00:48:49.460
Yeah, and Nargajuna says,
you can't find this starting.

00:48:49.460 --> 00:48:50.980
Okay, then there's no Michael.

00:48:50.980 --> 00:48:52.290
Okay! There's no Michael.

00:48:52.290 --> 00:48:53.990
Well then there's no karma, okay?

00:48:53.990 --> 00:48:55.180
Yeah, there's no karma.

00:48:55.180 --> 00:48:57.500
Well then why did you
bow down at the Buddha

00:48:57.500 --> 00:48:59.480
who taught karma at the first verse?

00:48:59.480 --> 00:49:00.573
Why, you crazy?

00:49:03.220 --> 00:49:06.320
And by the way, I'm not, it's not BS.

00:49:06.320 --> 00:49:07.153
It's deep.

00:49:07.153 --> 00:49:08.460
It's important.

00:49:08.460 --> 00:49:11.610
If you understand it,
your mantras will work.

00:49:11.610 --> 00:49:12.930
And if you don't understand it,

00:49:12.930 --> 00:49:15.240
maybe you get a little
power out of mantra,

00:49:15.240 --> 00:49:19.070
because of your faith, but
you won't get the full power.

00:49:19.070 --> 00:49:23.270
You'll get like one millionth of 1% power

00:49:23.270 --> 00:49:26.850
on the mantras if you don't
understand how they work.

00:49:26.850 --> 00:49:28.920
How does a mantra work?

00:49:28.920 --> 00:49:30.560
How does karma work?

00:49:30.560 --> 00:49:32.190
How does action work?

00:49:32.190 --> 00:49:33.740
When did the action start?

00:49:33.740 --> 00:49:34.910
Who did the action?

00:49:34.910 --> 00:49:36.380
What action did they start?

00:49:36.380 --> 00:49:38.110
When did the action start?

00:49:38.110 --> 00:49:39.840
Did the person doing
the action come first,

00:49:39.840 --> 00:49:41.400
or the action came first?

00:49:41.400 --> 00:49:43.330
If the action didn't come

00:49:43.330 --> 00:49:44.290
before the person who did the action,

00:49:44.290 --> 00:49:46.170
how can you call the
person who did the action

00:49:46.170 --> 00:49:50.610
a person who did the action,
because there's no action yet?

00:49:50.610 --> 00:49:51.833
Something's fishy.

00:49:53.420 --> 00:49:55.240
And it's not just crazy talk.

00:49:56.260 --> 00:49:59.790
There's a reason why this
book survived for 2,000 years.

00:49:59.790 --> 00:50:02.220
And there's a reason
why hundreds of people,

00:50:02.220 --> 00:50:05.630
hundreds of great people,
wrote commentaries.

00:50:05.630 --> 00:50:07.490
There's a reason.

00:50:07.490 --> 00:50:09.960
There's something
important about this book.

00:50:09.960 --> 00:50:11.580
Now, last thing.

00:50:11.580 --> 00:50:15.798
Oh by the way, we have a mom
and a daughter baking a cake.

00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:20.400
The mom and the daughter
who are making a cake,

00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:21.853
are they bakers right now?

00:50:23.530 --> 00:50:26.300
No, they're not bakers,
nothing's been baked yet.

00:50:26.300 --> 00:50:28.170
Give me a break.

00:50:28.170 --> 00:50:29.003
They're not bakers.

00:50:29.003 --> 00:50:32.370
They're just people with weird hats on.

00:50:33.530 --> 00:50:36.857
They're not bakers yet.
There's nothing baked.

00:50:36.857 --> 00:50:39.910
Until there's something baked,
you can't call them a baker.

00:50:39.910 --> 00:50:40.953
Got it?

00:50:41.840 --> 00:50:44.800
But how can you have a baked
thing without the baker?

00:50:44.800 --> 00:50:48.990
If the girl and her mom cannot be bakers

00:50:48.990 --> 00:50:51.330
until the cake is baked,

00:50:51.330 --> 00:50:55.653
because until then there's no
reason to call them bakers.

00:50:56.800 --> 00:50:59.370
But the cake can't bake itself.

00:50:59.370 --> 00:51:01.160
Somebody has to come and bake the cake.

00:51:01.160 --> 00:51:02.870
So the baker has to come before the cake.

00:51:02.870 --> 00:51:06.040
No, no, no, I just told
you. The baker can't come

00:51:06.040 --> 00:51:08.868
before the cake, because
the baker's not a baker

00:51:08.868 --> 00:51:09.701
until they bake something.

00:51:09.701 --> 00:51:12.190
Yeah, but I just told you
if they bake something,

00:51:12.190 --> 00:51:14.650
there's got to be someone
to bake it before that.

00:51:14.650 --> 00:51:18.260
There has to be a baker
before baked cake, right?

00:51:18.260 --> 00:51:22.460
No, no, no. You can't have
a baker before a baked cake,

00:51:22.460 --> 00:51:24.580
because until you have a baked
cake the baker's not a baker,

00:51:24.580 --> 00:51:28.348
because the baker didn't bake anything.

00:51:29.369 --> 00:51:30.620
And it's not a joke.

00:51:30.620 --> 00:51:33.340
And if you're going to
use Medicine Buddha mantra

00:51:33.340 --> 00:51:36.863
to stop cancer, then you
got to understand this.

00:51:40.694 --> 00:51:43.060
Which word in the mantra fixed the cancer,

00:51:43.060 --> 00:51:45.290
the first one or the last one?

00:51:45.290 --> 00:51:48.680
And which mantra was it,
number 10,000, or number 9,000?

00:51:48.680 --> 00:51:50.460
Which mantra worked?

00:51:50.460 --> 00:51:53.010
When did it work?

00:51:53.010 --> 00:51:53.850
What do you mean mantra?

00:51:53.850 --> 00:51:56.750
There is no mantra till something happens,

00:51:56.750 --> 00:52:00.370
otherwise it's just a sentence.

00:52:00.370 --> 00:52:04.240
You know, you can say banana
and if nothing happens,

00:52:04.240 --> 00:52:05.590
it's not a mantra.

00:52:05.590 --> 00:52:07.790
You can say OM MANI PADME HUM

00:52:07.790 --> 00:52:10.510
and if it doesn't do anything,
then it's not a mantra.

00:52:10.510 --> 00:52:13.770
A mantra does some miracle thing.

00:52:13.770 --> 00:52:16.430
Until there's a miracle,
you can't have a mantra.

00:52:16.430 --> 00:52:17.650
But if a miracle doesn't happen,

00:52:17.650 --> 00:52:20.100
you can't have a mantra either.

00:52:20.100 --> 00:52:21.263
Got it?

00:52:23.350 --> 00:52:26.253
Now last thing we have a few minutes left.

00:52:27.170 --> 00:52:31.830
This "Wisdom" text of Nargajuna

00:52:31.830 --> 00:52:35.500
is a great place to
learn a little Sanskrit.

00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:38.300
I call it, you know, what's it called?

00:52:38.300 --> 00:52:41.017
Get to know Sanskrit, or something.

00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:45.940
So if you want to learn some Sanskrit,

00:52:45.940 --> 00:52:47.298
which is what you're going to talk

00:52:47.298 --> 00:52:49.290
after you become a Buddha,

00:52:49.290 --> 00:52:51.593
so you better work on it now.

00:52:54.240 --> 00:52:55.710
Let's learn a little Sanskrit.

00:52:55.710 --> 00:52:57.230
This is the perfect book.

00:52:57.230 --> 00:53:00.400
The verses are short, sweet.

00:53:00.400 --> 00:53:02.640
If you want to learn Sanskrit,

00:53:02.640 --> 00:53:04.360
in the monastery they'd say,

00:53:04.360 --> 00:53:06.040
oh just memorize the book.

00:53:06.040 --> 00:53:08.200
It's not that hard.

00:53:08.200 --> 00:53:11.708
If you get in the habit of
memorizing, you can memorize.

00:53:11.708 --> 00:53:14.041
,GANG GIS RTEN CING 'BREL BAR 'BYUNG,

00:53:14.041 --> 00:53:16.482
,'GAG PA MED PA SKYE MED PA,
,CHAD PA MED PA RTAG MED PA,

00:53:16.482 --> 00:53:20.159
,'GRO MED PA 'ONG BA MED,
,THA DAD DON MIN DON GCIG MIN,

00:53:20.159 --> 00:53:23.468
,RDZOGS PA'I SANGS RGYAS SMRA RNAMS KYI,

00:53:23.468 --> 00:53:25.143
,DAM PA DE LA PHYAG 'TSAL
LO,, or something like that...

00:53:25.143 --> 00:53:27.140
You can memorize it.

00:53:27.140 --> 00:53:28.700
You can do it.

00:53:28.700 --> 00:53:30.910
So let's learn a few Sanskrit words.

00:53:30.910 --> 00:53:34.920
And here's the Sanskrit
words that we already learned

00:53:34.920 --> 00:53:36.480
in the first eight chapters.

00:53:36.480 --> 00:53:38.763
Okay, Tim, you got it for me?

00:53:40.590 --> 00:53:42.690
We're going to get to know Sanskrit.

00:53:42.690 --> 00:53:46.693
And the first word you should
learn is the name of the book.

00:53:47.670 --> 00:53:50.940
And it's very embarrassing
for your teacher

00:53:50.940 --> 00:53:52.607
when somebody asks you,
what are you studying?

00:53:52.607 --> 00:53:54.418
You say, I don't know,

00:53:54.418 --> 00:53:57.434
but I've been doing it for three years.

00:53:59.234 --> 00:54:01.000
Then Geshe-la feels embarrassed.

00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:02.700
So what book are you studying?

00:54:02.700 --> 00:54:05.107
Prajna. Say Prajna.

00:54:05.107 --> 00:54:05.940
- [All] Prajna.

00:54:05.940 --> 00:54:07.117
- [Michael] Prajna.

00:54:07.117 --> 00:54:07.950
- [All] Prajna.

00:54:07.950 --> 00:54:09.520
- So the J is not an
English J, it's a D-Z.

00:54:09.520 --> 00:54:12.437
The Russians are right.
It's na, prajna, prajna.

00:54:14.823 --> 00:54:16.280
And then there's a long A.

00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:17.840
The last A is a long A.

00:54:17.840 --> 00:54:19.950
The Tibetan is SHES RAB.

00:54:19.950 --> 00:54:22.920
It's a little bit of an E sound, SHES RAB.

00:54:22.920 --> 00:54:25.567
You don't say sharob. SHES RAB, SHES RAB.

00:54:27.123 --> 00:54:31.020
The Sanskrit word, we're going to learn

00:54:31.020 --> 00:54:32.820
to deconstruct a Sanskrit word.

00:54:32.820 --> 00:54:35.210
We're going to learn how to
break down a Sanskrit word

00:54:35.210 --> 00:54:36.820
into its parts.

00:54:36.820 --> 00:54:38.450
And then we're going to learn cognates,

00:54:38.450 --> 00:54:39.443
which is?

00:54:40.875 --> 00:54:42.781
(speaking off microphone)

00:54:42.781 --> 00:54:44.203
Yeah, related modern words.

00:54:45.470 --> 00:54:48.780
So pra- means to come in front.

00:54:48.780 --> 00:54:52.579
It comes in the English
words, proud, prow of a boat,

00:54:52.579 --> 00:54:54.210
the front of a boat, forward.

00:54:54.210 --> 00:54:58.400
So pra- means in front,
it becomes like supra,

00:54:58.400 --> 00:55:01.510
super, super good, super good.

00:55:01.510 --> 00:55:04.740
Okay, so pra- here means supra.

00:55:04.740 --> 00:55:06.137
And supra comes from pra-.

00:55:07.130 --> 00:55:08.110
Then we have the root.

00:55:08.110 --> 00:55:09.930
When you see that little
square root sign (√),

00:55:09.930 --> 00:55:14.183
it means a Sanskrit root
√jna and that means to know.

00:55:15.030 --> 00:55:20.030
And that's why there's a K
in the English word, know,

00:55:21.170 --> 00:55:26.170
because there used to be a
jna, jna and that came in

00:55:26.700 --> 00:55:31.223
to the English word
know, or gnostic, or ken.

00:55:32.297 --> 00:55:34.570
You know, is it beyond your ken or not,

00:55:34.570 --> 00:55:36.250
meaning your understanding.

00:55:36.250 --> 00:55:38.050
So √jna means to know.

00:55:38.050 --> 00:55:42.347
The Russians, you've got
the perfect verb, Знаю (,

00:55:42.347 --> 00:55:43.770
Я Знаю (Ya Znayu).

00:55:43.770 --> 00:55:46.030
Russian is much closer
to the original Sanskrit,

00:55:46.030 --> 00:55:47.480
because it's closer to Greek.

00:55:49.560 --> 00:55:52.370
Last thing to say about wisdom,
it has a feminine ending,

00:55:52.370 --> 00:55:53.553
long A, prajna, prajna.

00:55:56.520 --> 00:56:01.520
And generally wisdom is
considered a feminine aspect

00:56:01.980 --> 00:56:04.703
because it gives birth to
all kinds of good things.

00:56:05.720 --> 00:56:07.587
Let's do one more Sanskrit word

00:56:07.587 --> 00:56:09.840
and we're done with the class. Yay!

00:56:09.840 --> 00:56:11.480
I'm sorry the classes are so long

00:56:11.480 --> 00:56:13.910
and I'm not sorry you should sit there.

00:56:13.910 --> 00:56:17.105
Okay, say pariksha.

00:56:17.105 --> 00:56:18.470
- [All] pariksha.

00:56:18.470 --> 00:56:19.303
- Pariksha.

00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:22.380
So that means an investigation.

00:56:22.380 --> 00:56:25.460
And you know, you got to know this word

00:56:25.460 --> 00:56:28.340
if you're going to read
the 27 investigations,

00:56:28.340 --> 00:56:32.107
the 27 chapters of the
book called, "Wisdom".

00:56:32.961 --> 00:56:37.380
The book called "Prajna" has 27 parikshas.

00:56:37.380 --> 00:56:42.133
Pari- means all around,
like the perimeter.

00:56:43.150 --> 00:56:47.020
Generally A in Sanskrit
becomes an E in English.

00:56:47.020 --> 00:56:51.560
So pari- becomes peri- like
perimeter or periscope.

00:56:51.560 --> 00:56:53.430
So when you get in a
submarine and you look

00:56:53.430 --> 00:56:56.503
all around the ocean,
it's called a periscope.

00:56:57.750 --> 00:56:58.913
Pari-, all around.

00:57:00.265 --> 00:57:01.830
Iksha means to see.

00:57:01.830 --> 00:57:04.690
It's an ancient verb, to look.

00:57:04.690 --> 00:57:09.530
And there's a German word
auge, which comes from that.

00:57:09.530 --> 00:57:11.850
And then that came into English as ocular

00:57:11.850 --> 00:57:16.013
and even the word eye. So the
word eye comes from iksha.

00:57:16.996 --> 00:57:20.390
The eyeball comes from,
eye comes from auge,

00:57:21.260 --> 00:57:24.490
comes from iksha, which means to look.

00:57:24.490 --> 00:57:26.900
So when you look all around something,

00:57:26.900 --> 00:57:30.040
that's an investigation,
a pari- iksh, pariksha.

00:57:31.470 --> 00:57:33.510
Okay, so we're going to pariksha.

00:57:33.510 --> 00:57:36.920
So try to learn those few Sanskrit words.

00:57:36.920 --> 00:57:40.010
So far, we have prajna, wisdom,

00:57:40.010 --> 00:57:42.440
the name of Nargajuna's great book

00:57:42.440 --> 00:57:44.970
and pariksha, which is
crucial for the book.

00:57:44.970 --> 00:57:48.190
It's an investigation of different ideas.

00:57:48.190 --> 00:57:51.530
We are investigating, especially,

00:57:51.530 --> 00:57:53.950
why does the Medicine Buddha mantra work.

00:57:53.950 --> 00:57:57.920
And if you want it to
work better, or stronger,

00:57:57.920 --> 00:58:00.120
then understand its emptiness.

00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:02.170
Try to understand its emptiness.

00:58:02.170 --> 00:58:05.510
If you really understand its emptiness,

00:58:05.510 --> 00:58:10.510
the mantra can make you into a
being who can jump from world

00:58:12.620 --> 00:58:16.750
to world in a few
seconds, planet to planet,

00:58:16.750 --> 00:58:19.830
in a few seconds and help
billions of people each time.

00:58:19.830 --> 00:58:24.660
If you really understand
the emptiness of the mantra,

00:58:24.660 --> 00:58:26.280
it can make you a Buddha.

00:58:26.280 --> 00:58:29.190
Okay, cool. See you in the next class

00:58:29.190 --> 00:58:32.053
and we'll start our new chapter, nine.

